{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgb989nS4GXVCumbzFH8w","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I couldn't get the combined plan to pass. The binding needs your Keycloak user id, and I don't have it. I haven't applied anything.\n\n**What the platform said, in order:**\n1. **Namespace:** it refused `metadata.namespace: t6025-full` on the RoleBinding and said RoleBinding lives in namespace `org`. The Role stays in `t6025-full`. I fixed this.\n2. **Subject:** it refused `user: owner@example.invalid` (PF-126). A person must be named by their Keycloak user id, a UUID, and never by e-mail, because Git keeps every e-mail for good.\n\n**What I tried:**\n- The member list, which shows user ids, was refused earlier because I can't read RoleBindings in this project.\n- I haven't made up a UUID. A made-up id would either fail or grant the role to someone else.\n\n**Plan as it stands:**\n- **Role:** `data-reader` with `ContextSpace` and `Endpoint` read. It still leaves out `DataModel`, which the platform refused earlier.\n- **RoleBinding:** `data-reader-owner` in namespace `org`, role `data-reader`, scope project `t6025-full`, with your user id as the subject. That one field is still missing.\n\n**What I need from you:** your Keycloak user id. It's in the Portal's account or profile page, or a project admin can read it from the member list. Send it and I'll re-plan right away. I'll also ask again whether to keep `DataModel` out of the role."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":586,"cache_read_input_tokens":34917,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":586},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c6486bfb-fa96-40df-8d52-